# Copilot instructions for @@project_name@@

The full rules are in `AGENTS.md` (read it). This is the short form, for tools that
read only this file, such as code review; it must stay under about 4,000 characters.

@@#if monorepo@@- A monorepo; each component has its own stack and gate (`sh scripts/quality.sh --changed` runs those a branch changed):
@@components_digest@@
- Commit scopes are the component names, or `deps`, `docs`, `ci`, `release`.
@@/if@@@@#unless monorepo@@- Stack: @@label@@.@@#if src_dir@@ Code in `@@src_dir@@/`@@#if test_dir@@, tests in `@@test_dir@@/`@@/if@@.@@/if@@ Gate: `@@quality_cmd@@`.
@@/unless@@- Never commit to `@@default_branch@@`; work on a branch (`feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `chore/`) and open a pull request.
- Commits and pull request titles follow Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject`, types `feat fix perf refactor docs test build ci chore style revert`, imperative subject, header at most @@header_max@@ characters, one concern per commit.
@@#if spec_driven@@- Behaviour changes update the spec first (`openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md`). The `no-spec` label is only for changes with no behaviour change: a test needing a new case or a changed number or message means the behaviour changed.
@@/if@@@@#unless spec_driven@@- A significant architectural choice gets a decision record in `docs/adr/`; read the existing records before changing what they cover.
@@/unless@@- Tests go with the code; they never call a paid or external service for real.
- Update the docs the change makes stale (README, `docs/ENGINEERING.md`, `ROADMAP.md`).
- Do not read, print or commit secrets or `.env`. Do not skip hooks or weaken checks.
- Review: flag a behaviour change with no test or spec, a skipped check, a secret, an unrelated refactor, a missing decision record for an architectural choice.
@@#if no_attribution@@- No attribution trailers or generated-by footers in commits or pull request text.
@@/if@@- Say what was verified and what was not.
